{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"evaluated":9,"overflow":0,"schema":"epic_bug_screen_v1","tally":[{"citation":"Bug describes a defect in ticket state-machine cascade logic (reopen/claim/transition); RP-04 epic concerns operation-scoped configuration, provider auth composition, and credential handling—no overlap with ticket lifecycle or parent/child status invariants.","ticket_id":"a392-f630-7b25-4b14","title":"reopen lacks the parent-first cascade that claim/transition have, allowing a closed parent with an open child","verdict":"C"},{"citation":"RP-04 S2/S3 cut reconciler read/check paths to operation runtimes; close_precheck._check_file_impact_vs_diff is a completion gate that must execute within the scoped runtime binding and survive packaging/import resolution.","ticket_id":"08c8-2236-376f-435e","title":"Packaged rebar release omits _engine_support/commit_impact.py, breaking every close with file_impact","verdict":"A"},{"citation":"RP-04 AC: 'backends stop reloading' and 'fail closed when explicit provider/profile/project/auth composition fails; never retry anonymously' — preview/dry-run must not perform remote writes, but run_differs.py recovery lacks persist/mode guard on client.add_label/set_entity_property calls that RP-04's scoped-runtime binding contract should enforce.","ticket_id":"7851-e06b-9e85-4c9e","title":"Preview and dry-run passes perform remote Jira writes during pending-binding recovery","verdict":"A"},{"citation":"Bug describes a pre-existing test-coverage gap in binding_lifecycle that RP-02 S2 T2 exposed; RP-04 does not own binding_lifecycle or its test oracle, only operation-scoped config/auth composition and runtime bindings.","ticket_id":"02c4-4e64-5ee3-459c","title":"Idempotency oracle no longer reaches moved binding clock reads","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"BindingRepository lifecycle alerts are RP-02 S1 T1 extraction work (deliberately pinned pre-existing behavior); RP-04 owns operation-scoped config/auth composition and provider bindings, not binding-store alert deduplication.","ticket_id":"8384-f31f-f16f-4f14","title":"Binding lifecycle alerts never dedupe - records omit timestamp_ns","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"RP-04 S7.4 generates operator docs from registries and drift checks; this bug is a pre-existing documentation gap in identity setup that predates the epic's config/auth composition work and falls outside the approved scope of RP-04's generated docs (which cover precedence, lifecycles, provider ownership, and deliberate deltas, not identity creation prerequisites).","ticket_id":"cd53-c62e-7bac-4ed2","title":"Setup docs omit rebar identity create --self before signing gates","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"RP-04 S1 'Compose immutable operation snapshots' and AC 'a captured operation is stable across environment/file/cwd mutation' — the bug describes a defect in operation lifetime isolation where concurrent tool reinstall invalidates the active process's resolved release, violating the immutability and stability contract the epic's snapshot composition must enforce.","ticket_id":"559b-b7cd-6552-437d","title":"Concurrent uv tool reinstall can delete the active rebar release during a gate invocation","verdict":"A"},{"citation":"Root disk pressure and review-bot health are pre-existing infrastructure/deployment concerns; RP-04 addresses operation-scoped config/auth composition and does not claim to change disk management, snapshot GC thresholds, Docker cache pruning, or host resource monitoring.","ticket_id":"3a52-2d79-320d-4fed","title":"[root-disk-pressure] Root disk reaches 90% and review-bot drops unhealthy after automated-reclaim mitigation","verdict":"B"},{"citation":"RP-04 S3 'Cut reconciler apply and child processes to scoped runtimes' requires reconciler apply paths to use operation-scoped bindings; standalone concurrency loader's inability to import git_adapter violates the immutable runtime binding contract and blocks the cutover of reconciler apply to scoped runtimes.","ticket_id":"b0a8-5496-d178-40a9","title":"Standalone concurrency loader cannot import git adapter","verdict":"A"}],"ticket_id":"e215-ab23-ed6a-4791"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMPLETION_VERDICT","timestamp":1787172032797595001,"uuid":"c16af5a0-8ba4-4b6c-866d-3fe8a0d6c2ca"}